# The sbx document toolkit's Python environment (07.17.1.1.1 D-03, D-09; ADR-0043): the libraries a bot's sandbox
# uses to read PDFs, Office files, sheets, images (OCR through tesseract), HTML/XML and text of unknown encoding,
# installed by the image into the pip-less venv /opt/ocw-tools/venv with `--require-hashes --no-deps --only-binary
# :all:` from requirements.lock.
#
# Top-level names only, unpinned. `tools/lock.sh` is the only way to update requirements.lock (it resolves inside the
# image's pinned base with its Python 3.11.2, wheels only); never edit the lock by hand. A pin held back by the
# 14-day rule of `scripts/sandbox-lock-evidence.mjs` is written here as `name<version` with the run date.
#
# Removed from D-03 (D-09): extract-msg (GPL, and a GPL/LGPL tree of about eight more pins; Debian `msgconvert` plus
# the stdlib `email` parser read .msg), odfpy (sdist only, refused by `--only-binary :all:`; LibreOffice reads ODF),
# chardet (charset-normalizer covers it and is already a pdfminer.six dependency), PyMuPDF (AGPL/commercial), xlrd
# (its LICENSE adds a four-clause BSD-style text with an advertising clause, outside the allow list; dropped on
# 2026-11-12 by the orchestrator: `ocw-extract` reads legacy .xls through LibreOffice, 07.17.1.1.1-03).
# held back by the 14-day rule on 2026-11-12 (7.0.0 uploaded 2026-11-06, 7.0.1 on 2026-11-10)
pypdf<7.0.0
pdfplumber
python-docx
openpyxl
python-pptx
# held back by the 14-day rule on 2026-11-12 (3.1.1 uploaded 2026-11-04)
pandas<3.1.1
Pillow
pytesseract
charset-normalizer
beautifulsoup4
lxml
defusedxml
# Dependencies listed only to hold them back by the 14-day rule on 2026-11-12 (pdfplumber needs pypdfium2, pandas
# needs python-dateutil): pypdfium2 5.15.0 uploaded 2026-11-06 (5.15.1 yanked, 5.15.2 on 2026-11-09), python-dateutil
# 4.0.0 uploaded 2026-11-01. Drop a line once its newer version passes the rule.
pypdfium2<5.15.0
python-dateutil<4.0.0
